# Reserved-control spellings, one per line, driven through every guard copy
# and deny profile by tests/test-reserved-control-spellings.sh.
#
# Columns are whitespace-separated and the spelling is the rest of the line:
#   act tier policy queue ready worker-guard tower-guard worker-profile tower-profile spelling
#
# tier: any, worker, or tower. policy: `floor` (no value permits the act) or
# <knob>=<value>, where `unresolved` means no value resolves yet, so some copy
# must deny. A floor line is tier `any` and denied by both profiles and by the
# tower queue. Verdicts: deny, defer, or n/a (outside the copy's jurisdiction:
# another tier, or a tool the copy is not wired for); the test derives n/a from
# the wiring and fails a line that claims it anywhere else.
#
